## What is *not* bundled here

ctbench additionally contains four fixtures derived from the
[picorv32](https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32) project by Claire Wolf, which remain
under the upstream **ISC** licence: `pcpi_div.v`, `pcpi_mul.v`, `pcpi_div_wiped.v`,
and `pcpi_div_halfwipe.v`.

**None of those four ship in this Space.** They are *unscored* in ctbench — their
observable is a secret-residue property rather than a completion signal — and this
demo bundles only the 18 scored fixtures. If you need them, take them from the
[ctbench repository](https://github.com/nickharris808/ctbench), where the full ISC
notice travels with them in `LICENSE-FIXTURES`.
